is  a  driver for the IDEC Supervision/16, an image capture board
that plugs into a 16‐bit ISA bus.  The IDEC Supervision/16  digi‐
tizes an NTSC television signal, storing a 512 x 480‐pixel, 8‐bit
grayscale  image in its 256kB dynamic RAM array every 1/30th of a
second.  The host reads frames from the DRAM using 122881  16‐bit
I/O reads.  Reading frames from the Supervision/16 is quite slow:
after  the  host  reads a 16‐bit word from the DRAM, the Supervi‐
sion/16 state machine takes approximately 0.5 microseconds to get
ready for the next read.  Theoretically, a frame rate of approxi‐
mately 10 frames per second is possible.  achieves a  frame  rate
